                        "entry_id": "e68edf04-37e9-3d89-8886-78e144634666",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Domination des terres ; puissance fondée sur la domination de la terre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Relations internationales"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "821bc220-6e4b-3468-b127-ba4f99181b6e",
                        "entry_id": "e68edf04-37e9-3d89-8886-78e144634666",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Domination des terres ; puissance fondée sur la domination de la terre.",
                            "État, empire, société dont la puissance politique réside dans la domination des terres."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "metonymically"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "032176a2-eee9-4a91-8794-9f8f2284af85",
                                "sense_id": "821bc220-6e4b-3468-b127-ba4f99181b6e",
                                "text": "Cette opposition à une Europe atlantique fait ressurgir les théories de Karl Schmitt sur les conflits de la tellurocratie et de la thalassocratie."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "da3d4f0b-19f1-464b-82e6-4dcc70848210",
                                "sense_id": "821bc220-6e4b-3468-b127-ba4f99181b6e",
                                "text": "On pourrait résumer les choses par cette formule : thalassocratie américaine contre tellurocratie chinoise. Reste que cette configuration est en train d'évoluer, la Chine cherchant aujourd'hui à défendre ses intérêts en développant une marine marchande et militaire […]."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "94e99bf8-298b-4cae-b213-065813b7aa78",
                        "source_entry_id": "e68edf04-37e9-3d89-8886-78e144634666",
                        "target_lang_word": "Tellurokratie",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "69684e11-8f1a-4152-8792-f91f3782a845",
                        "source_entry_id": "e68edf04-37e9-3d89-8886-78e144634666",
                        "target_lang_word": "tellurocracy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tellurocracy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "451ef5d6-0762-3d0a-95eb-68a82524bcfa",
                                        "entry_id": "5109391b-5e97-3a94-b2d4-e00740cb3068",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dominance or supremacy due to military or commercial power on land."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e291651-7da2-4d15-a9c2-18794fb59b25",
                                                "sense_id": "451ef5d6-0762-3d0a-95eb-68a82524bcfa",
                                                "text": "Probably the United States has realized, a bit too late, that its stake on a pro-Pakistan regime in Afghanistan had been a mistake. Obviously, this was done not for the sake of stake itself: the strategic aim was to penetrate the Heartland. From the point of view of the tellurocracy versus thalassocracy opposition a maritime power (the US) may entrench itself in the IRAFPAK zone."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6368d58-7f20-4365-a16e-6519089fc713",
                                                "sense_id": "451ef5d6-0762-3d0a-95eb-68a82524bcfa",
                                                "text": "Historically, Russians did not immediately realize the significance of their location and only accepted the baton of tellurocracy after the Mongolian conquests of Ghengis Khan, whose empire was a model of tellurocracy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb462b7e-3928-466c-8bf8-e54ec54888a4",
                                                "sense_id": "451ef5d6-0762-3d0a-95eb-68a82524bcfa",
                                                "text": "A union of Russia and several different Asian countries would represent the cultural values of tellurocracy, in opposing the movement toward neo-liberal globalization that is at the center of the constellation of maritime powers that is guided by the United States."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a17d4e8e-8b26-3cdc-9a48-ae0be8b7dd4d",
                                        "entry_id": "5109391b-5e97-3a94-b2d4-e00740cb3068",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A state whose power derives from landbased military or commercial supremacy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77578693-ed86-4b62-bb43-b32d66ad1c6c",
                                                "sense_id": "a17d4e8e-8b26-3cdc-9a48-ae0be8b7dd4d",
                                                "text": "The \"thalassocracy\" here is the United States and its allies; the \"tellurocracy\" is Eurasia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "30b63db2-18b1-45d7-81b9-8a649b93d856",
                                                "sense_id": "a17d4e8e-8b26-3cdc-9a48-ae0be8b7dd4d",
                                                "text": "In his works Dugin draws the picture of an ancient confrontation between the Atlantic oceanic powers (\"talassocracies\"), whose roots go back to the drowned continent of Atlantis and which are headed today by the mondialist United States, and the Eurasian continental powers (\"tellurocracies\"), whose roots lie in the mythical country of \"Hyperborea,\" the most important of which today is Russia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8cf8db8-190d-42bf-b642-826638cbd172",
                                                "sense_id": "a17d4e8e-8b26-3cdc-9a48-ae0be8b7dd4d",
                                                "text": "If thalassocracies are defined as democratic, commercial and pragmatic, tellurocracies are ideocratic, with a hierarchical organization and guided by a religious ideal."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
